	\subsection{Full Extraction Diagnostics}
	
	To check whether the implemented text-extraction stages can support the stronger terrain-aware workflow, we ran GiNZA extraction over all 33,378 records without calling any public geocoding API. This diagnostic is not a final accuracy evaluation, but it exposes extraction coverage and geocoding workload before a full local or cached Nominatim run. Across the full dataset, 9,361 records (28.1\%) received at least one place mention, while 20,242 records (60.6\%) received at least one terrain term. The extracted terrain terms were frequent enough to affect downstream classification: after re-running terrain enrichment with the extracted terrain fields, the full dataset contained 17,983 coastal, 10,151 plain, 4,056 mountain, 861 valley, and 327 inland-water records.
	
